{
 "result": "Built `squeeze.py` providing exact round-trip `compress(bytes) -> bytes` and `decompress(bytes) -> bytes` using only the Python standard library (`lzma`, `json`, `re`, `collections`), paired with `bench.py` which generates a deterministic 703,963-byte benchmark mix of English-like paragraphs and structured JSON records. `squeeze.py` applies a lossless reversible preprocessor\u2014detecting and transposing homogeneous JSON object arrays into columnar layout, splitting structured hyphenated fields, and dictionary-tokenizing frequent words into single-byte high-bit tokens with capitalization markers\u2014followed by raw LZMA1 compression (`PRESET_EXTREME`, `lc=3, lp=0, pb=0, nice_len=273`) and a fallback safety check guaranteeing 100% lossless round-trip across empty bytes, single bytes, full 0..255 binary data, English text, JSON, and the combined dataset, improving the compression ratio from the 7.19x baseline to 10.61x (66,341 compressed bytes).",
 "calls": 20,
